  "details": "Only some avatars have this problem with holoport. Two examples of default public avatars that exhibit this are Beach Ball Boy and Nana the Clownfish.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n1. Stand on an elevated platform and hold holoport to walk off it onto a lower platform.\n\nIssue: The camera frequently resets to the vertical position of the avatar head as its position changes during holoport locomotion.\n\n2. Release holoport.\n\nIssue: When the camera snaps back to the head, the difference in height is added once again the head height, pushing the avatar head and camera into the floor and distorting the body.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\n1. The camera should never change world relative position while holoport is held.\n\n2. Holoport release should not affect the position of the avatars head relative to the ground.\n\nThis issue has been present for a long time. It only occurs with FBT disabled and does not occur with FBT enabled.",
